# Example: build and run hello

File: cli/examples/hello.oot

The smallest full trip: one file, two commands, one line out.

## The file

Save this as `hello.oo`:

```
// # Hello — First cli Trip
//
// Logline: Print one line. Proves build and run work.
//
// Setup: No outside files. No network. Runs anywhere.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Build with cli. Run with cli. See one line.
```

`cli build hello.oo` turns it into a program.
`cli run hello.oo` builds it and runs it at once.

## What you should see

The run prints its greeting line and stops with no errors.
Exact words depend on your file. Silence plus an error line
means the build failed: read the first error line, it names
the problem and the file.

## Try next

- `cli fmt hello.oo --check` — asks if the layout is tidy.
- `cli context .` — lists every `.oo` file in this folder.
- `cli fix hello.oo` — only needed when the build complains.
